# {name}

A movement for the MPX-Dog.

```bash
mpx-cli deploy         # build, upload and run — the usual loop
mpx-cli logs -f        # what the robot is saying
```

## Editing it

`src/{name}.{ext}` is the whole skill. `on_start()` runs once; the optional
`on_stop()` runs when it ends, so you can leave the robot somewhere sensible.

## Parameters

`manifest.json` declares the knobs. Change one without rebuilding:

```bash
mpx-cli run --param reach=25 --param repeats=2
```

The robot's web UI reads the same declarations and renders a control for each.

## Where things are

There is no `include/` here on purpose. The SDK headers live in exactly one
place — `sdk/include/` in the SDK checkout — and `mpx-cli` points the compiler
at them. Vendoring a copy per project is how you end up with a header that
quietly describes a different ABI than the robot is running.

